\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Compatible resistance sequences}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{For each integer #{n\ge 0} let #{V_n} be a finite set,
injected into #{V_{n+1}}. Identify #{V_n} with its image, and
write #{V_*} for the union. On #{V_n} let a connected graph
have a positive conductance on each edge. The associated
nonnegative Laplacian is
##{(L_nu)(x)=\sum_{y\sim x}c_{xy}\bigl(u(x)-u(y)\bigr),}
and the energy is
##{E_n(u)=\sum_{\mathrm{edges}}c_{xy}\bigl(u(x)-u(y)\bigr)^2.}
The kernel of #{L_n} is the constant functions. The sequence
is a \newvocab{compatible resistance sequence} when, for every
#{u} on #{V_n},
##{E_n(u)=\min\bigl\{E_{n+1}(v):v|_{V_n}=u\bigr\}.}
The minimum runs over real functions on #{V_{n+1}}.}
